       Question
  The Nautilus DevOps team needs to set up several docker environments for different applications. One of the team members has been assigned a ticket where he has been asked to create some docker networks to be used later. Complete the task based on the following ticket description:

 1-Create a docker network named as blog on App Server 2 in Stratos DC.
 2-Configure it to use macvlan drivers.
 3-Set it to use subnet 10.10.1.0/24 and iprange 10.10.1.0/24.

        Solution
 1- Login into app server 2
       ssh steve@stapp02
  - create the Docker network
      docker network create blog -d macvlan --ip-range 10.10.1.0/24 --subnet 10.10.1.0/24
  - To verify
      docker network ls
